{title: 538 - Guide Me, O Thou Great Jehovah}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #538 • CWM RHONDDA • 8.7.8.8.8.7.7}
{lyricist: William Williams}
{composer: John Hughes}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 538}
{meta: tune CWM RHONDDA}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.8.8.7.7}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Guide [C]me, [Bm]O [D/A]Thou [G]great Jehovah,
[G]Pilgrim [C]through [Am]this [G/D]barren land.
[G]I [C]am [Bm]weak, [D/A]but [G]Thou art mighty;
[G]Hold [C/E]me [Bm]with [C]Thy powerful [G]hand.
[D7]Bread of heaven, [G]bread [D7]of [G]heaven,
[G/B]Feed me till I [Em]want no [D]more;
[Bm]Feed [D7/A]me [G]till I [C]want [G/D]no [D7]more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Open [Bm]now [D/A]the [G]crystal fountain,
[G]whence the [C]healing [G/D]stream [D7]doth [G]flow;
[G]let [C]the [Bm]fire [D/A]and [G]cloudy pillar
[G]lead [C/E]me [Bm]all [C]my journey [D]through.
[D7]Strong deliverer, [G]strong deliverer,
[G/B]be thou still my [Em]strength and [D]shield;
[Bm]be [D7/A]thou [G]still my [C]strength [G/D]and [D7]shield.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]When [C]I [Bm]tread [D/A]the [G]verge of Jordan,
[G]bid my [C]anxious [G/D]fears [D7]subside;
[G]death [C]of [Bm]death [D/A]and [G]hell's destruction,
[G]land [C/E]me [Bm]safe [C]on Canaan's [D]side.
[D7]Songs of praises, [G]songs [D7]of [G]praises,
[G/B]I will ever [Em]give to [D]thee;
[Bm]I [D7/A]will [G]ever [C]give [G/D]to [D7]thee.
{end_of_verse}
